@AuthUserService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5100

### US-08: Dispatcher registers their own account (public - no token)
POST {{AuthUserService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register/dispatcher
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "dispatcher.one",
  "email": "dispatcher.one@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "firstName": "Dina",
  "lastName": "Perera",
  "contactNumber": "0771234567"
}

### US-08 Scenario 2: missing/invalid fields -> 400 with per-field errors
POST {{AuthUserService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register/dispatcher
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short",
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "",
  "contactNumber": "12"
}

### US-08 Scenario 4: log in with the registered credentials -> JWT with role Dispatcher
POST {{AuthUserService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "dispatcher.one",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}
